<title>SPAIN: Spain's Puleva-Uniasa posts '96 profit vs '95 loss.</title>
<headline>Spain's Puleva-Uniasa posts '96 profit vs '95 loss.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-02-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>1996 results for Spain's Puleva-Uniasa in billions of pesetas, unless stated:</p>
<p> Net attributable profit/loss	2.72     vs   -0.081</p>
<p> Pretax profit/loss		    2.72     vs   -0.081</p>
<p> Net turnover			   23.56     vs   20.78</p>
<p> Operating profit			1.10     vs   -0.082</p>
<p> Ordinary profit			 1.81     vs   0.822</p>
<p> Financial income			0.967    vs   1.28</p>
<p> Extraordinary profit		  0.883    vs  -0.903</p>
<p>NOTE: Puleva said operating results improved after a restructuring plan, a 12.7 percent rise in net turnover and the greater proportion of sales of value-added products.</p>
<p>Financial income fell because of lower interest rates and a reduction in the firm's cash surplus, it said.</p>
<p>-- Madrid Newsroom, + 341 585 8340</p>
</text>
